ace):\n\n0 + 0 = 0.\n\nNext, tens place: 6 + 0 = 6.\n\nHundreds place: 4 + 1 = 5.\n\nThousands place: 3 + 9 = 12. Write down 2, carry over 1 to the next column (ten thousands).\n\nTen thousands place: 2 + 8 = 10, plus the carried over 1 makes 11. Write down 1, carry over 1 to the next column (hundred thousands).\n\nHundred thousands place: 7 + 1 = 8, plus the carried over 1 makes 9.\n\nPutting it all together, the sum is 912,560.\n\nWait, let me confirm:\n\nLet me add the thousands place again:\n\n3 (thousands from first number) + 9 (thousands from second number). Since each is in the thousands place, so 3,000 + 9,000 = 12,000. So that gives 2 in thousands place and carryover 1 to ten thousands.\n\nTen thousands place: 2 (ten thousands from first number is 20,000) + 8 (ten thousands from second number is 80,000) = 100,000. Adding the carried over 1 (which is 10,000) gives 110,000. So we write 1 in the ten thousands place and carry over 1 to hundred thousands.\n\nHundred thousands place: 7 (700,000) + 1 (100,000) = 800,000 plus the carried over 1 (100,000) gives 900,000. Thus, 9 in the hundred thousands place.\n\nSo combining all digits:\n\nHundred thousands: 9\n\nTen thousands: 1\n\nThousands: 2\n\nHundreds: 5 (Wait, earlier I had 4 +1 =5 in hundreds place)\n\nTens: 6\n\nOnes: 0\n\nWait, so the number would be 912,560?\n\nWait, let me check each digit again step by step.\n\nLet me write the numbers aligned:\n\n723460\n\n+189100\n\n--------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes place: 0 + 0 = 0.\n\nTens place: 6 + 0 = 6.\n\nHundreds place: 4 + 1 = 5.\n\nThousands place: 3 (from 723,460's thousands digit is 3?) Wait, hold on, let's confirm the digits in each number.\n\nFirst number is 723,460:\n\nDigits from right: 0 (ones), 6 (tens), 4 (hundreds), 3 (thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 7 (hundred thousands).\n\nSecond number is 189,100:\n\nDigits from right: 0 (ones), 0 (tens), 1 (hundreds), 9 (thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 1 (hundred thousands).\n\nSo when adding:\n\nOnes