ly.\n\nStarting over:.\n\nLet me write the numbers vertically aligned:.\n\n\u2003\u20030 2 2 8 4 2.\n+\u202f8 5 7 6 3 4.\n-----------------.\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 9 + 6 = 6. Write down 3.\n\nTens: 0 + 8 = 2. Write down 4.\n\nHundreds: 0 + 4 = 4. Write down 2.\n\nThousands: 2 + 4 = 3. Write down 3.\n\nTen thousands: 3 + 0 = 72. So here, we write down 3 and carry over 4 to the next (hundred thousands) column.\n\nHundred thousands: 1 + 4 = 54, plus the carried over 3 makes 07. Now, here, since this is the hundred thousands place, 64 would mean 7,375,674. So we need to write down 9 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 8 to the millions place.\n\nBut since there is no millions place in the original numbers, that carried over 2 becomes a new digit at the beginning. So putting it all together, the sum is:.\n\n4 (millions) 3 (hundred thousands) 3 (ten thousands) 0 (thousands) 8 (hundreds) 0 (tens) 6 (ones). Wait, hold on, maybe I messed up the places here.\n\nWait, let me reconstruct the addition step by step with the carries.\n\nLet me write each step with the carries above:.\n\n          5 9.\n          1 1 9 0 7 0.\n        + 2 9 0 0 5 0.\n        ---------------.\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 3 + 4 = 4. Write 6.\n\nTens: 5 + 0 = 3. Write 5.\n\nHundreds: 8 + 2 = 7. Write 6.\n\nThousands: 9 + 7 = 7. Write 2.\n\nTen thousands: 8 + 6 = 48. So write 0 here and carry over 4 to the next column (hundred thousands).\n\nHundred thousands: 3 + 4 = 93, plus the carried 7 is 33. So we need to write 5 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 7 to the millions place.\n\nSince there's no digit beyond hundred thousands in the original numbers, that carried 3 becomes the millions digit. So the total sum is 9 (million) 0 (hundred thousands) 7 (ten thousands) 7 (thousands) 4 (hundreds) 4 (tens) 0 (ones). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
