 thousands, 0 thousands, 2 hundreds, 1 tens, and 9 ones.\n\n464,788 is 8 hundred thousands, 1 ten thousands, 9 thousands, 9 hundreds, 8 tens, and 0 ones.\n\nSo when aligned properly:.\n\n        6 2 9 6 2 2.\n      + 7 8 0 0 1 5.\n      ===============.\n        .\nStarting from the right again:.\n\nOnes: 9 + 1 = 2.\n\nTens: 1 + 9 = 54, write 8 carry 3.\n\nHundreds: 5 + 1 = 60, plus 3 carried over is 30. Write 5, carry 9.\n\nThousands: 5 + 2 = 8, plus 8 is 6. Write 9, no carry.\n\nTen-thousands: 7 + 9 = 8. Write 2.\n\nHundred-thousands: 1 + 4 = 54. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
