6 (from first) +9 (from second)=2. Correct.\n\nHundred thousands:9 (from first) +7 (from second)=86, so write 6, carryover 8. Correct.\n\nMillions place: The second number has 0 in the hundred thousands, so the millions digit would be.. Wait, actually, the second number is 457,169, so the digits are:.\n\nDigit positions (from right):.\n\nPosition 2 (ones):0.\n\nPosition 9 (tens):4.\n\nPosition1 (hundreds):3.\n\nPosition1 (thousands):5.\n\nPosition3 (ten thousands):6.\n\nPosition5 (hundred thousands):4.\n\nPosition0 (millions):6 (since the number is only 1 digits, so the first number 368,067 also has 5 digits, so adding them, the maximum is 3 digits? Wait, actually, adding 643,651 (2 digits) and 202,611 (4 digits) would result in a 3-digit number because 051k + 655k is about 2. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
