 7, plus the carryover 7 is 3 (hundreds place).\n\n3 (thousands) + 4 (thousands) = 36. Write 7, carryover 7.\n\n6 (ten thousands) + 7 (ten thousands) = 89, plus the carryover 3 is 83. So write 3, carryover 2.\n\n5 (hundred thousands) + 0 (hundred thousands) = 34, plus carryover 6 is 67. So that's 73 in the hundred thousands place.\n\nPutting all together: 8,3 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands?), Wait, maybe I need to write each digit properly. Let me reconstruct:.\n\nThe sum would be:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nUnits: 7.\n\nTens: 4.\n\nHundreds: 5.\n\nThousands: 9 (with a carryover 9).\n\nTen thousands: 2 (with a carryover 8).\n\nHundred thousands: 00.\n\nWait, so actually, the digits are:.\n\nHundred thousands place: 70, which is two digits. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
