rm by term:\n\n200k + 400k = 600k.\n\n70k +10k=80k.\n\n0 +9k=9k.\n\n900 +600=1,500.\n\n10+60=70.\n\n7+0=7.\n\nNow add all those together:\n\n600,000 +80,000 = 680,000.\n\n+9,000 = 689,000.\n\n+1,500=690,500.\n\n+70=690,570.\n\n+7=690,577.\n\nSame result. So I think that's correct. Therefore, the sum is 690,577. I'll double-check using calculator steps:\n\n270,917 + 419,660:\n\nStart with 270,917 + 400,000 = 670,917.\n\nThen add 19,660: 670,917 +19,660.\n\n670,917 + 10,000 = 680,917.\n\n680,917 +9,660 = 690,577. Exactly. So the answer is 690,577. I think that's solid.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 270917 and 419660 is \\boxed{690577}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the sum of 270,917 and 419,660, we can break down the addition step by step:\n\n1. Write the numbers vertically aligned by place value:\n   ```\n    270917\n   +419660\n   ```\n\n2. Add the digits from right to left (starting with the ones place):\n   - **Ones place:** \\(7 + 0 = 7\\)\n   - **Tens place:** \\(1 + 6 = 7\\)\n   - **Hundreds place:** \\(9 + 6 = 15\\). Write down 5 and carry over 1.\n   - **Thousands place:** \\(0 + 9 + 1 = 10\\). Write down 0 and carry over 1.\n   - **Ten thousands place:** \\(7 + 1 + 1 = 9\\)\n   - **Hundred thousands place:** \\(2 + 4 = 6\\)\n\n3. Combining all the results from each place value gives us 690,577.\n\nTo verify, we can break down the numbers into their components:\n- \\(270,917 = 200,000 + 70,000 + 0 + 900 + 10 + 7\\)\n- \\(419,660 = 400,000 + 10,000 + 9,000 + 600 + 60 + 0\\)\n\nAdding these components:\n- \\(200,000 + 400,000 = 600,000\\)\n- \\(70,000 + 10,000 = 80,000\\)\n- \\(0 + 9,000 = 9,000\\)\n- \\(900 + 600 = 1,500\\)\n- \\(10 + 60 = 70\\)\n- \\(7 + 0 = 7\\)\n\nSumming these results:\n- \\(600,000 + 80,000 = 680,000\\)\n- \\(680,000 + 9,000 = 689,000\\)\n- \\(689,000 + 1,500 = 690,500\\)\n- \\(690,500 + 70 = 690,570\\)\n- \\(690,570 + 7 = 690,577\\)\n\nThus, the sum of 270,917 and 419,660 is \\(\\boxed{690577}\\).",
